<title>USA: U.S. cash soymeal - Some rail basis offers higher.</title>
<headline>U.S. cash soymeal - Some rail basis offers higher.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-04-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Some offers for rail and truck soymeal in U.S. cash markets were higher Monday in response to expectations for tight near-term supplies, U.S. dealers said.</p>
<p>&quot;Some people are taking downtime--scheduled or unscheduled--or they are covering orders for other people,&quot; a dealer in the southeast said.</p>
<p>One dealer in Indiana said that his supply of soymeal had tightened dramatically, so he was not offering rail soymeal for the next several days.</p>
<p>&quot;We're tight here,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>&quot;There's no meal on track here like I heard they have in Illinois,&quot; the Indiana dealer added.</p>
<p>Another Midwest dealer said the market was still firm following a burst of buying activity from processors last week.  </p>
